          "score": 7.5,
          "severity": "high",
          "method": "CVSSv31",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
        }
      ],
      "cwes": [
        674
      ],
      "description": "Apache XmlSchema doesn't limit how deeply schema imports and includes can be nested, so a malicious schema can make parsing recurse until the stack overflows. This causes a denial of service.\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes this issue.",
      "published": "2026-09-29T12:17:09Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-06T14:38:53Z",
      "analysis": {
        "state": "not_affected",
        "justification": "code_not_reachable",
        "detail": "This vulnerability affects a component which is a transitive dependency of Apache CXF, and is only applicable when CXF is used to consume untrusted WSDLs. This never occurs in this case (consumption of SOAP, WSDL-based services), rendering this finding non-exploitable."
      },
      "affects": [
        {
          "ref": "4e4d1240-628a-4610-b77c-6ad7be3f8012"
        }
      ]
    },
