      "cwes": [
        674
      ],
      "description": "Apache XmlSchema doesn't limit how deeply schema structures can be nested when it builds its schema model, so a malicious schema can make parsing recurse until the stack overflows. This causes a denial of service.\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes this issue.",
      "published": "2026-09-29T12:17:09Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-06T14:38:42Z",
      "analysis": {
        "state": "not_affected",
        "justification": "code_not_reachable",
        "detail": "This vulnerability affects a component which is a transitive dependency of Apache CXF, and is only applicable when CXF is used to consume untrusted WSDLs. This never occurs in this case (consumption of SOAP, WSDL-based services), rendering this finding non-exploitable."
      },
      "affects": [
