          "score": 7.5,
          "severity": "high",
          "method": "CVSSv31",
          "vector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
        }
      ],
      "cwes": [
        674
      ],
      "description": "The Apache XmlSchema walker (xmlschema-walker) doesn't detect cycles in type derivation, substitution groups, model groups or attribute groups. A malicious schema with such a cycle can make the walker recurse until the stack overflows, causing a denial of service.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 2.3.3, which fixes this issue.",
      "published": "2026-09-29T12:17:09Z",
      "updated": "2026-10-06T14:37:44Z",
      "analysis": {
        "state": "not_affected",
        "justification": "code_not_reachable",
        "detail": "This vulnerability affects a component which is a transitive dependency of Apache CXF, and is only applicable when CXF is used to consume untrusted WSDLs. This never occurs in this case (consumption of SOAP, WSDL-based services), rendering this finding non-exploitable."
      },
      "affects": [
